invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the doubling leaves out the masked move, so twice the point at
  infinity comes out as (0 : 0 : 0). That names no point, and a complete
  addition that reads it gives (0 : 0 : 0) back whatever it adds, while
  an affine conversion reads it as the point at infinity, since its Z is
  zero. bin/p256_equiv_test doubles the point at infinity and requires
  (0 : Y : 0) with Y not zero.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_cmov(&y3, &p256_wide_fe_one_mont, p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->z));
--- new
